<article class="env-definition" id="011G">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/011G">Definition <span data-tag="011G">12.14.7</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{A}$ be an additive category. Let $A^\bullet $ be a cochain complex with boundary maps $d_ A^ n : A^ n \to A^{n + 1}$. For any $k \in \mathbf{Z}$ we define the <em>$k$-shifted cochain complex $A[k]^\bullet $</em> as follows: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
we set $A[k]^ n = A^{n + k}$, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
we set $d_{A[k]}^ n : A[k]^ n \to A[k]^{n + 1}$ equal to $d_{A[k]}^ n = (-1)^ k d_ A^{n + k}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> If $f : A^\bullet \to B^\bullet $ is a morphism of cochain complexes, then we let $f[k] : A[k]^\bullet \to B[k]^\bullet $ be the morphism of cochain complexes with $f[k]^ n = f^{k + n}$. </p>
</article>